# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: a method's body reads g, which nothing declares or passes -- "unresolved
# name" is said at g, where the free name stands (the text its record keeps), not at the method's line.
fn: f () int
    int: t 0
    t: g + 1
return: t
int: ok 0
ok: f()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
